A||||1||Carrolles||C-500 wire color help?||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||09-22-2000||08:39 AM||||I'm in the process of straightening out the wiring mess on my new (to me) 85GT.  Apparently the previous owner replaced the engine and the wiring harness is a mess.<P>I started at the C-500 connector and found that the wire colors don't match my 85 Helms manual diagrams.  I guess the engine harness is from another year car.<P>Does anyone have Helms manuals for the 86, 87, and 88.  If so would you mind giving me the color wire for each pin location on the engine harness side of the C-500 connector along with the circuit number?  My Helms has a table showing pin number with wire color and circuit number.  This helps in tracking the wiring diagrams.<P>Mine has a very large yellow wire instead of the purple called for in my Helms.  It also has a large red wire that he had grounded to the intake plenum.  I haven't disturbed the black goo on the connector enough to see which wire is attached to which pin yet.<P>These would be the pins in rows A through E.<P>I was able to drive the car when I got it so whatever he did worked.  I'm just trying to put it all back together to look nice.  I've re-loomed most of it (at least what I can get to without removing the intake).<P>The dog bone bracket was broken at the exhaust manifold because he did not install the bracket that attaches it to the front head.  Also the battery support is basically dust.  I cut out the old remnants and have the new one in place.  I bolted it to the fender well so far.  This weekend I'll finish bolting it to the fender and the front firewall.<P>I got the missing brackets for Ed Parks and from a local wrecking yard.  So far everything is going together nicely.  I've had to remove just about every bracket and mount to straighten out cross threaded bolts and replace missing ones.  My tap and die set has gotten a real workout so far.<P>TIA,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric_PA||09-22-2000||09:44 AM||||Check this site out for schematics. <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm</A>  there is a link at the bottom of this page.<P>Eric<BR>86.5 GT<P><BR>||||reg||1
